  "Notes": "Uniform quarter-wave stack ABA...A (Sec. IV, Fig. 5) with the same number of layers and the same peak stop-band attenuation as equal-ripple case A, for comparison\nSpecification: Peak attenuation equal to case A (Line 4: 13.59 dB).\nReported: Table II Line 16 (p. 309), case A: n1/n2 = 1.267; bandwidth to first nulls (fractional, in theta/90) 0.26; first attenuation ripple height 1.0 dB; first reflectance ripple height 0.2; peak attenuation designed equal to 13.59 dB (Line 4). Recomputed here with n1, n2 to 3 decimals: 13.41 dB, nulls bandwidth 0.258, first reflectance ripple 0.18 (0.87 dB).\nNotes: 19 layers alternating n1 (odd layers, both outer layers) and n2, all quarter waves at reference_nm (arbitrary 550 nm; the paper uses theta/90). End media n_0 = 1 on both sides (\"n_0 = 1 in each case\"); n1*n2 ~ 1. Normal incidence. Small differences from the printed attenuation come from the 3-digit indices.\nLayers from Table II Line 16(a)-(e), p. 309; text Sec. VI.F p. 308-309; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours 13.41 dB at the centre; paper 13.59 dB, the equal-ripple design it is matched to (indices printed to 3 figures).",
